  "notes": "This contract records the portable C++ TCK check for the standard lookahead-control boundary. Each Requirements Lab API surface is listed separately and pinned by its canonical 2025 API-surface ID. The source uses only the official IEEE 1516.1 C++ RTIambassador and FederateAmbassador APIs plus the standard library; the adapter supplies the provider package, FOM, endpoint, logical-time implementation, and callback configuration. It verifies the pre-regulation query and modification failures, the initial Query Lookahead value, a valid Modify Lookahead increase, InvalidLookahead rejection for an incompatible official standard interval representation, a gradual decrease from three epsilon to two and then one epsilon over successive grants, and a deferred decrease to zero at its grant boundary. It does not assert provider-specific callback timing, MOM reports, DDM, save/restore, or interoperability.",
